burrito literally means little donkey it  is the sliced bread of food that is not  sliced bread where did the burrito begin  where any burrito begins with fit  tortilla tortillas originally made from  corn have been used by early  Mesoamericans from the Mayans to the  Aztecs they would fill their tortillas  with chili peppers tomatoes mushrooms  squash and avocado the influence of the  Spanish in the 1500s  gave birth to the flour tortilla the  perfect tortilla to create a burrito  but the burrito would not appear for  another 400 years the 19th century  Vaqueros of northern Mexico would fill  their tortillas with machaca dried  shredded beef frodo burritos the legend  of the named burrito comes from Ciudad  Juarez where one Mendes would deliver  tortilla wrapped meals on his little  donkey in the 1930s the burrito makes  its first appearance on a restaurant  menu in Los Angeles in the 1960s  burritos added to the English dictionary  around the same time as the first taco  bell it should also be noted during this  period that the world's most popular  rock band was formed and we successfully  embarked on the first manned mission to  the moon we're not saying burritos  created modern pop music and  interstellar travel we're also not not  saying that the 70s was the height of  burrito experimentation San Francisco  developed the mission burrito then there  was the San Diego marina meanwhile in  New Mexico the breakfast burrito in the  1980's Taco Bell invented the Kayseri  dough but it was too mind-blowing for  simpler times in the 90s with the  widespread popularity of grunge music  there were a few advancements chili  cheese burritos had some success but  they disappeared along with stonewash  Keens beanbag chairs blacklight posters  and tongue rings by the year 2000 the  quesadilla burrito medley was a sad  fantasy best leftist science fiction  conventions and KX theorists but that  didn't stop humanity from dreaming we  invented burrito vending machines Korean  BBQ inspired burritos and tiny burritos  fruit  and finally the world was ready for the  keys there you have it the evolution of  the burrito  you
 

